From f2327d39bed4192f3120c66828eab425823cf53e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sixvolts <rigel@sixvolts.org>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:45:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: MoE decode chain on GCN: fused down+reduce, q8 emit
 from gate/up, Q8_0 LDS-staged nc, loads-first Q8_0 matvecs

Flash-Next (qwen4exp, 4x MI50) decode and short-batch work, all measured in-model:

- mul_mat_vec_q5_1_repacked_down_reduce<R>: the MoE down projection (one token) with the
  router-weighted expert sum folded in; thread -> (expert slot, sub-block), R rows per block,
  LDS reduction writes the mixed row. Hooked in ggml_cuda_try_fuse ahead of the MUL_MAT_ID
  op when the moe weighted-reduction pattern follows; ids are copied aside when the
  allocator put the output on the dead routing buffer. 25.6 + 5.9 us -> 29.3 us per layer and
  43 fewer launches/token. Env GGML_CUDA_DOWN_REDUCE_R (default 4, 0 = off).
- mul_mat_vec_q5_1_repacked_pack<DOWN_R,HAS_IDS> (crossport R4): thread-packed short-row
  down kernel for the multi-token (verify) path, 28.7 -> 25.5 us at 1 row, 70.9 -> 61.6 at 3.
  Env GGML_CUDA_Q5_1_DOWN_R (default 4, 0 = SEG kernel).
- mul_mat_vec_q4k_repacked_glu16_q8: the gate/up GLU kernel also writes its outputs' q8_1
  blocks for the down projection (32 rows per 512-thread block = one block of outputs), via
  ggml_cuda_repack_xq_emit_target now accepting a MUL_MAT_ID consumer in its padded per-row
  layout. quantize_q8_1 launches 101 -> 54 per token, bit-identical. GGML_CUDA_NO_GLU16_Q8.
- mul_mat_vec_q8_0_repacked_lds_nc<NC,4> (crossport R2): activations staged in LDS per
  32-sub-block chunk, half a sub-block per lane, 4 rows per wave; summation order of the
  1-column kernel (KLD 0). Dispatched for 4..8 columns: pp6 Q8_0 17.3 -> 14.6 ms/step
  (126.6 -> 134 tok/s), pp5 +4%, pp3/pp4 level. GGML_CUDA_NO_Q8_LDS_NC.
- 9..32 columns on matrices <= 64M weights (MTP eh_proj flattened over n_hc x tokens) run as
  column chunks of <= 8 through the staged kernel instead of the tile GEMM (417 us) or the
  generic 16-column kernel (303 us). GGML_CUDA_NO_Q8_NC_CHUNK.
- Loads-first variants (crossport R10) of the Q8_0 multi matvec (73.6 -> 68.5 us) and the
  shared-expert Q8_0 GLU (10.2 -> 8.7 us), same arithmetic. GGML_CUDA_NO_Q8_MULTI_UNROLL,
  GGML_CUDA_NO_Q8_GLU_UNROLL. A sched_barrier after the hoisted loads and a split-K variant
  measured no gain and are not included.
- GGML_CUDA_REPACK_TRACE=1 logs every repacked dense matmul's shape; GGML_CUDA_FUSE_DEBUG=1
  reports why the down+reduce fusion did not apply.

Together with the rank top-k: tg64 50.1 -> ~51.5-52 (bench spread +-0.4), greedy MTP output
unchanged, ub1 KLD at the model's reorder noise floor for the non-bit-identical kernels.

